# Roth Project Guide (Tier 2)

Roth conversion calculator, and the Auth.js host (`/api/auth`). Plans, users,
sessions, and invites live in one MongoDB (`MONGODB_DB`). Deep architecture
and engine rules live in
[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Prefer that file for math and engine work.
Use this guide for UI, product features, and the index below.

## Layout

| Area | Path | Notes |
| ---- | ---- | ----- |
| App shell | `src/app/` | Served at `/`. `CalculatorHome` hosts calculator + modals. Auth.js at `src/app/api/auth`, branded errors at `src/app/auth/error` |
| Auth | `src/lib/auth/` | Auth.js config, mail, invites, auth UI. Route re-exports `handlers` |
| Shared UI, legal, email | `src/lib/common/` | Footer, legal docs, site URLs, Mailgun send |
| Plan UI | `src/components/plan/` | Name modal, multi-step plan modal, summary |
| Wizard steps | `src/components/wizard/steps/` | Steps rendered inside `PlanModal` |
| UI store | `src/store/useUI.ts` | Modals, first-run, drafts |
| Scenario store | `src/store/useScenario.ts` | Plans hydrate/save, household edits |
| Domain | `src/lib/domain/` | Pure household rules (e.g. untouched check) |

## Project invariants

- Invite and auth constants live in `src/lib/auth/shared`. Import them. Do not
  re-declare them.
- Friendly UI copy: no em dashes, and no hyphen used as a sentence separator.
- Plans, Auth.js collections (users, sessions, accounts, invites), and
  external data all live in `MONGODB_DB` (project `.env`). Required:
  missing throws. Restart `next dev` after changing DB env.
  `src/lib/db/connection.ts` stays free of `server-only` because
  `scripts/invalidate-sessions.ts` loads it through `users.ts` outside
  Next.js. App code imports `@/lib/db/mongo`.
- `EXTERNAL_DATA_API_URL` is the app origin (`http://localhost:3000`). A path
  on that URL is ignored. A stale port makes seed/check miss the app and the
  browser GET 404s until Mongo is seeded.
- Never list a server-only key in `nextConfig.env`. Those keys are compiled
  into the bundles as string literals.
- The app is the whole site: calculator, Auth.js (`/api/auth`), and
  `/api/dev/login`. Plan URLs are `/{publicId}`. App origin is `AUTH_URL`.
  Auth.js also needs `AUTH_SECRET` and `AUTH_TRUST_HOST`. Invite and share
  links use that origin in development and the canonical domain in production.
- Magic-link send does not create an Auth.js user. `createUser` runs only
  after they click the link. Login / register screen switches must not reset
  the email step.

